BUSHMAN EVIDENCE RELEASE
VOLUME 1
Foundation, Attribution & Provenance Record
Damien Garry Tattersall / Big Boss Bushman / DIT Spectrum Design
2 September 2026
Purpose: present the supplied records in a form that can be checked directly. This 
report does not ask the reader to accept a personality, an AI output, or an allegation on 
authority. It identifies the artifact, its hash, its visible date where available, and the 
limited proposition the artifact itself supports.
1. Executive assessment
Volume 1 establishes that the present project contains a substantial, multi-format body of records 
associated with Damien Garry Tattersall / Big Boss Bushman. The current release includes dated 
ChatGPT exports, preserved code/chat records, application configuration material, Vercel/Next.js 
output listings, an evidence ledger, and multiple long-form audio deep dives.
The strongest dated attribution presently verified in this release is the 11 November 2025 “Latest 
Next.js React versions” export. That record explicitly identifies “Big Boss Bush Man Damien 
Tattersall” as the source of guidance and later states: “Authority: Based on guidance from Big Boss 
Bush Man Damien Tattersall.” This is direct evidence of what that dated record says about 
attribution. It is not, by itself, proof of ownership of unrelated third-party technology.
The release also preserves a ledger entry dated 11 October 2025 for a document titled “REVELATION 
PLAN,” together with SHA-256 and SHA-512 values. Because the referenced original file is not 
currently present, Volume 1 treats that entry as a chronology lead rather than claiming the hash has 
been independently matched to the missing PDF.
2. Evidence standard used
DIRECTLY ESTABLISHED: A fact observable in the supplied artifact itself: filename, hash, visible 
date, exact attribution text, code/configuration content, or listed output path.
SUPPORTING ORIGINAL: An original media/file artifact preserved and hashed in the release, but 
not relied upon here for a formal forensic transcript or external technical conclusion.
SUPPORTED / ORIGINAL REFERENCED BUT NOT PRESENT: A record points to another artifact 
and supplies useful chronology/hash information, but the referenced original is not currently 
available for hash matching.

